; ASL's top-level `note` -- a free-standing string bound to nothing, legal
; between declarations -- is retired: the host now rejects it with
; ERR_READ_BARE_TOPLEVEL, the same as ASN always did. Prose that used to live
; in a note belongs in the package's doc.asn now, not in the source file.
;
; ASN never had the note reading to begin with: a document is one value and a
; bare string IS a value, so a note beside a payload is simply a second
; document, not prose. This is why `;` stays the only annotation ASN has.
"A note, which is a declaration in the language and a second document here."
(:sku "SSD-1TB" :price 89.99)
